# The service worker must never be served from cache. A stale sw.js pins an old
# app shell on a rep's phone and there is no way for them to force an update
# from the field.
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate

/manifest.webmanifest
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# Build assets are content-hashed, so a given URL's contents can never change —
# which is the textbook case for `immutable` and a one-year max-age. Both are
# deliberately absent here, because that combination caused a real outage.
#
# Pages answers a request for an asset it has not finished propagating with the
# SPA fallback: index.html, content-type text/html, status 200. This rule is what
# decided how long that wrong answer would live. At a year with `immutable`, the
# stylesheet for a whole deployment was served as a brotli-compressed HTML
# document from the edge — status 200, nosniff correctly refusing to apply it,
# every screen unstyled — and a purge-by-URL could not evict it because
# `Vary: accept-encoding` had split it into variants.
#
# Five minutes means the same mistake heals itself before anyone finishes
# reporting it. The cost is near zero: repeat loads never reach this layer at all,
# because the service worker serves assets from Cache Storage, which does not
# consult the HTTP cache. Offline support comes from the worker, not from here.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300

# Applied to every page. The app loads nothing from another origin except the
# map — no CDN, no analytics, no third-party fonts of its own — so the policy
# names hosts explicitly rather than opening a category. Anything else the app
# tried to reach would be a bug or a compromise, and either way should fail.
#
# api.maptiler.com appears in both `img-src` and `connect-src`: the first for the
# tiles themselves, the second because the service worker *fetches* them to cache
# for offline use, which is a fetch rather than an image load.
#
# The Google hosts are what the Maps JavaScript API needs, and they are not
# guessable from the docs alone — each one is here for a specific reason:
#
#   maps.googleapis.com     the bootstrap script, the tile and metadata requests
#                           it makes afterwards, and Street View Static images.
#   maps.gstatic.com        the secondary scripts and sprites the API pulls in.
#   fonts.googleapis.com    Maps injects a stylesheet link for Roboto. Without
#                           this the map renders with fallback type; harmless,
#                           but it produces a console error on every load, and a
#                           console full of noise is where real errors go to die.
#   fonts.gstatic.com       the font files that stylesheet points at.
#   *.ggpht.com and
#   *.googleusercontent.com Street View imagery is served from these.
#   worker-src blob:        vector maps run their rendering in a worker created
#                           from a blob URL. Without this the map is blank with
#                           no network error to explain it.
#
# Deliberately NOT added: 'unsafe-eval'. Some CSP guides list it for Maps and it
# is not required for the parts this app uses. If a future Maps feature does need
# it, that is a decision to take explicitly — it re-enables eval for the entire
# application, and this app handles credentials and customer records.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://maps.googleapis.com https://maps.gstatic.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://api.maptiler.com https://maps.googleapis.com https://maps.gstatic.com https://*.ggpht.com https://*.googleusercontent.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; connect-src 'self' https://allstar-api.josh-af6.workers.dev https://api.maptiler.com https://maps.googleapis.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(self), camera=(self), microphone=(self), payment=(), usb=()
